<% content_for :page_title, "Add schools and study sites" %>

<%= content_for(:before_content) do %>

  <%= govuk_breadcrumbs(breadcrumbs: [
      govuk_breadcrumb_link_to("Home", root_path),
      govuk_breadcrumb_link_to("How to use this service", how_to_use_this_service_path),
      govuk_breadcrumb_link_to("Course summary examples", add_schools_and_study_sites_path),
    ]) %>

<% end %>

<div class="govuk-grid-row">
  <div class="govuk-grid-column-two-thirds">
    <h1 class="govuk-heading-l">
      <span class="govuk-caption-l">How to use this service</span>
      Add schools and study sites
    </h1>

    <h2 class="govuk-heading-s">Contents</h2>

    <ul class="govuk-list app-list--dash course-contents govuk-!-margin-bottom-8">
      <li><%= govuk_link_to "Showing placement schools to candidates", "#showing-schools" %></li>
      <li><%= govuk_link_to "Adding a school to your account", "#adding-a-school" %></li>
      <li><%= govuk_link_to "Adding a study site to your account", "#adding-a-study-site" %></li>
      <li><%= govuk_link_to "Attaching schools and study sites to a new course", "#attaching-schools-and-study-sites-to-a-new-course" %></li>
      <li><%= govuk_link_to "Attaching schools and study sites to an existing course", "#attaching-schools-and-study-sites-to-an-existing-course" %></li>
      <li><%= govuk_link_to "Detaching schools and study sites from a course", "#detaching-schools-and-study-sites-from-a-course" %></li>
      <li><%= govuk_link_to "Removing schools and study sites from your account", "#removing-schools-study-sites" %></li>
      </ul>

    <p class="govuk-body">
      60% of searches on Find teacher training courses are by city, town or postcode, so it’s important that location details have been added so courses can be found easily in searches.
    </p>

    <div class="govuk-warning-text">
      <span class="govuk-warning-text__icon" aria-hidden="true">!</span>

      <strong class="govuk-warning-text__text">
        Your courses will not appear in candidates’ location searches if you do not attach placement schools to them.
      </strong>
    </div>

    <p class="govuk-body">
      If you have any questions about adding schools and study sites, please email us at <%= govuk_mail_to bat_contact_email_address %> and we can assist you.
    </p>

    <h2 id="showing-schools" class="govuk-heading-m">Showing placement schools to candidates</h2>

    <p class="govuk-body">
      By default, schools attached to courses are hidden from candidates, and they cannot select a preferred placement school when applying for courses.
    </p>

    <%= image_tag("organisation-details-placements.png", class: "how-to-use-this-service-image") %>

    <p class="govuk-body">
      To allow candidates to see the placement schools attached to courses and select a preferred placement school, go to the 'Organisation details' tab and select 'Change' in the 'School placements' section.
    </p>

    <%= image_tag("show-placement-schools.png", class: "how-to-use-this-service-image") %>

    <h2 id="adding-a-school" class="govuk-heading-m">Adding a school to your account</h2>

    <p class="govuk-body">
      To add a school to your account, go to the ‘Schools’ tab and select ‘Add school’ or ‘Add multiple schools’.
    </p>

    <%= image_tag("add-schools.png", class: "how-to-use-this-service-image") %>

    <p class="govuk-body">
       You can add schools using their name or their unique reference number (URN). You can only add schools that are on <a href="https://get-information-schools.service.gov.uk/Search?SelectedTab=Establishments" class="govuk-link">Get Information About Schools (GIAS)</a>.
    </p>

    <%= image_tag("add-school.png", class: "how-to-use-this-service-image") %>

    <h2 id="adding-a-study-site" class="govuk-heading-m">Adding a study site to your account</h2>

    <p class="govuk-body">
      A study site is the location where the trainee will do the theoretical part of their training, for example a university campus.
    </p>

    <p class="govuk-body">To add a study site to your account, go to the 'Study sites' tab and select ‘Add study site’.</p>

    <%= image_tag("study-sites.png", class: "how-to-use-this-service-image") %>

    <p class="govuk-body">You can add study sites using their name or their unique reference number (URN). If you cannot find the study site, you can enter it manually.</p>

    <%= image_tag("add-study-site.png", class: "how-to-use-this-service-image") %>

    <h2 id="attaching-schools-and-study-sites-to-a-new-course" class="govuk-heading-m">Attaching schools and study sites to a new course</h2>

    <p class="govuk-body">When you add a new course, you’ll be asked to select all the school placements and study sites that apply.</p>

    <p class="govuk-body">On school direct salaried and apprenticeship courses, placement schools are referred to as ‘Employing schools’.</p>

    <%= image_tag("school-placements.png", class: "how-to-use-this-service-image") %>

    <p class="govuk-body">The ability to select all schools to be added to a new course is currently not available for new courses. </p>

    <p class="govuk-body">However, after you have created your new course, you will be able to edit it, and select all schools, if needed.</p>

    <h2 id="attaching-schools-and-study-sites-to-an-existing-course" class="govuk-heading-m">Attaching schools and study sites to an existing course</h2>

    <p class="govuk-body">To attach schools and study sites to an existing course, go to the ‘Basic details’ tab and select the ‘Change’ link next to ‘School placements’ or ‘Study sites’.</p>

    <%= image_tag("course-basic-details.png", class: "how-to-use-this-service-image") %>

    <p class="govuk-body">Select each school placement or study site that applies. Use 'Select all schools' to attach all schools to a course.</p>

    <%= image_tag("select-all-schools.png", class: "how-to-use-this-service-image") %>

    <p class="govuk-body">You can also update the schools attached to many courses at once. When adding or removing schools from a course, you will be asked if you want to apply that change to any other courses.</p>

    <%= image_tag("update-multiple-courses.png", class: "how-to-use-this-service-image") %>

    <h2 id="detaching-schools-and-study-sites-from-a-course" class="govuk-heading-m">Detaching schools and study sites from a course</h2>

    <p class="govuk-body">
      If you want to detach a school or study site from a course, you can select the change links as described, untick the check box and update.
    </p>

    <p class="govuk-body">
      If there are no places left at a school or the study site is no longer available, you can detach it from a course. If a place becomes available, you can simply attach it again.
    </p>

    <p class="govuk-body">
      If you need to remove a school or a study site from your account entirely, you’ll need to go to the ‘Schools’ or ‘Study sites’ tab to do this.
    </p>

    <h2 id="removing-schools-study-sites" class="govuk-heading-m">Removing schools and study sites from your account</h2>

    <p class="govuk-body">
      To remove a school, go to this list of schools in your account and select ‘Remove school’ next to the school’s name.
    </p>

    <p class="govuk-body govuk-inset-text">
      You will not be able to remove a school if it is the only placement school attached to a course. You must attach a different placement school to the course before you can remove the school from your account.
    </p>

  <p class="govuk-body">
      To remove a study site, select the study site from the list of study sites in your account and select ‘Remove study site’.
    </p>

    <p class="govuk-body govuk-inset-text">You will not be able to remove a study site if it has been attached to a course. You’ll need to <%= govuk_link_to "detach it from the course", "#detaching-schools-and-study-sites-from-a-course" %> first before you can remove it.</p>

  </div>
</div>
